# tools/t/tlb_reach_witness.rish -- the translation census refuses what it says it refuses, and
# the probe it drives still compiles.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/t/tlb_reach_witness.rish
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. The elder footprint study measured a table's cost against how many BYTES it
# touches and named the boundary worth designing to. A load's address is translated before any
# cache is asked, translations are cached in a structure whose capacity is counted in PAGES, and
# nothing in a byte count reaches that second bound. Measured on this pier 20260906: a walk over
# 64 pages costs 1.65 ns per dependent read and the same walk over 65 costs 3.90 ns -- same bytes
# touched, same instructions, same L1d sets, one more page. Handing that walk 2 MiB pages returns
# the ratio to 1.00, which is how the cause is known.
#
# WHAT THIS RUNG PROVES, and it is deliberately narrower than what the census measures.
#
#   The census refuses correctly. Thirty-two behaviors in a throwaway pen: seven legs shown from
#   the failing side, the argument handling shown the same way, and the clean baseline asserted
#   twice -- once before any plant and once after all of them, which is what proves the pen
#   innocent rather than merely quiet. Every plant is checked to have CHANGED the reading it was
#   applied to, so a mutation that silently fails to take is a FAULT rather than a skip.
#
#   The probe compiles. `--build-only` builds tools/fixtures/t/tlb_reach_probe.rye through the
#   census's own build path and stops.
#
# WHY THE BUILD LEG IS HERE AT ALL. REDS %449 found a module that had not compiled since the
# toolchain moved while four rostered guards read it every lap with grep, and %463 counted 178
# authored .rye files no build reaches. An unrostered census would leave this probe in exactly
# that set. Nineteen seconds buys the answer.
#
# WHAT THIS RUNG DOES NOT PROVE, and the omission is the design rather than a gap. It does not run
# the census on metal. That reading -- 64 pages, 256 KiB of span -- is a property of the BOARD,
# so a guard asserting it would red on the day this fleet moves to a different part, and a guard
# that reds on ordinary work is a guard someone turns off. The number travels as a measurement
# anyone can retake in about two minutes:
#
#   sh tools/fixtures/t/tlb_reach_census.sh
#
# Paper: external-research/20260906-061229_the-address-that-does-not-fit.md
# Elder: external-research/20260906-042838_the-table-that-fits.md

say "tlb-reach: Language EN -- a table is bounded twice, by bytes and by pages."
say "tlb-reach: Style Gauge, Meter -- the reach is measured on the board, never recited here."
say "tlb-reach: Lens TAME -- the pair is a control before it is a timer; say why."

let probe_here = run ["sh" "-c" "test -f tools/fixtures/t/tlb_reach_probe.rye"]
assert probe_here.ok else "tlb-reach: the probe is missing -- tools/fixtures/t/tlb_reach_probe.rye"

let census_here = run ["sh" "-c" "test -f tools/fixtures/t/tlb_reach_census.sh"]
assert census_here.ok else "tlb-reach: the census is missing -- tools/fixtures/t/tlb_reach_census.sh"

let control_here = run ["sh" "-c" "test -f tools/fixtures/t/tlb_reach_control.sh"]
assert control_here.ok else "tlb-reach: the control is missing -- tools/fixtures/t/tlb_reach_control.sh"

# The refusals, every one shown from the failing side, and the welcomes asserted as hard.
let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/t/tlb_reach_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "tlb-reach: the control refused -- read its FAULT lines"
assert control.out contains "faults 0" else "tlb-reach: the control reported a failing case"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict proven" else "tlb-reach: the control did not reach a verdict"
say "GREEN: tlb-reach -- every leg bites from the failing side, and the pen is proven innocent."

# A plant that changed nothing tests nothing. The control says so per plant; this pins the habit
# so a future edit that quietly stops mutating a reading cannot pass as proof.
assert control.out contains "plant took effect" else "tlb-reach: no plant was confirmed to have taken effect"
say "GREEN: tlb-reach -- each plant is proven to have changed the reading it was applied to."

# The probe still compiles. This is the rung REDS %449 and %463 paid for, in nineteen seconds.
let built = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/t/tlb_reach_census.sh" "--build-only"]
assert built.ok else "tlb-reach: the probe no longer builds -- an authored .rye nothing compiles is how %449 began"
assert built.out contains "build_only green" else "tlb-reach: the build leg reported no green"
say "GREEN: tlb-reach -- the probe compiles on this toolchain, so it is not a file nothing reaches."
